    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to present 80 Ennafort Park to the market. This wonderfully spacious five bedroomed home with garage is located in this much sought after area, which has long been a popular choice for growing families. Boasting well-appointed and light filled accommodation throughout, this home benefits from a fantastic, south-facing, very private rear garden. \n \nHaving been well cared for over the years, accommodation extends to approx. 154 Sq m/ 1,658 sq ft comprising of a welcoming, bright entrance hall, living room, dining room, breakfast room, and kitchen. Upstairs, there are 4 double bedrooms and a single bedroom. Two of the double bedrooms share a 'Jack & Jill' style shower room and there is also the main shower room (wet room). To the front the driveway provides for off-street parking in addition to the original garage and a covered side passage way leads to the beautiful sunny south facing rear garden. \n \nEnnafort enjoys a most convenient location just off the Howth Road. The location is second to none with Raheny, Killester and Clontarf villages all within easy access, and as a result there is an abundance of amenities to choose from. There is an excellent choice of national and secondary schools close by, as well as a huge choice of sporting and recreational facilities. St Anne's Park and stunning coastal walks and Dollymount beach are very close by. The property is just a short walk to Harmonstown and Raheny DART station, as well as numerous bus routes which provide easy access around the city.\n \nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate this fine family home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - 2.28m x 5.40m\nVery spacious hallway with under stairs storage, carpet, alarm panel\n\nLiving Room - 3.92m x 3.63m\nTo front, with open tiled fireplace, carpet, accordion-style opening into dining room\n\nDining Room - 3.92m x 3.63m\nTo rear, marble and wood surround fireplace with electric fire insert, TV point, sliding doors to south facing garden\n\nBreakfast Room - 3.51m x 3.31m\nCarpet, sliding door to garden, shelved storage press, door to kitchen\n\nKitchen - 3.25m x 4.10m\nL-shaped kitchen with selection of floor and wall cabinets, built-in electric grill and oven, dishwasher, gas hob and extractor fan, plumbed for washing machine and space for fridge/freezer, tiled floor, door to garden\n\nLanding - \nCarpet, hatch to attic with pull down Stira\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.93,m x 3.66m\nDouble to rear with built-in wardrobes, carpet\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.60m x 3.68m\nDouble to front with built-in wardrobes, carpet\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.28m x 4.29m\nDouble to rear, carpet\n\nEnsuite (Jack & Jill) - 1.78m x 1.50m\nElectric shower and wash hand basin with storage press, fully tiled, extractor fan\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.84m x 4.62m\nDouble to front, carpet\n\nShower Room - 2.28m x 1.63m\nFully tiled wet room to rear with shower, w.c., wash hand basin, heated towel rail, recessed lights\n\nGarage - 2.80m x 4.50m\nUp and over door opening to garage\n\nBoiler Room - 1.84m x 1.54m\nAccess from outside, covered side passage - location of gas boiler\n\nFront Garden - \nWalled and gated, with cobblelock drive way and lawn with mature planting\n\nBack Garden - \nVery private, walled and sunny south-facing rear garden mostly laid in lawn with mix of trees, hedging and mature shrubs\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Spacious 5 bedroomed semi-detached home</li><li>Private South-Facing Rear Garden</li><li>Garage and off-street driveway parking</li><li>Gas fired central heating</li><li>Double glazed windows</li><li>Approx. 154 sq.m. (1,658 sq.ft.)</li><li>Walking distance to DART and bus</li><li>Excellent schools in vicinity</li><li>Shops, supermarkets, cafes and restaurants in abundance nearby</li><li>St. Anne's Park and Dollymount Beach nearby</li><li>Dublin Airport approx.20 mins</ul>"
      },
      {
